Subject: [PATCH 5/7] Review: a ring another rank still holds is not measured;
 '0.3 wall cells'; the parallel test counts labels and sides

- The gathered path should leave no shared vertex on a cavity ring that meets
  the wall (none in 144 placements at 2-3 ranks), but that rests on the reach
  arithmetic. A ring that still has one is refused through the failure
  gather instead of measured on part of itself.
- The wording is '0.3 wall cells'.
- tests/parallel/test_0904 also asserts, over the ranks, that every outer-wall
  edge keeps its label and that FaultPlus and FaultMinus hold equal counts.
- test_0904: a unit test of the gate with one faked shared vertex.

Underworld development team with AI support from Claude Code
